# Module Boundaries

Imports between `studio/src/bifrost/`, `studio/src/components/`, and `studio/src/modules/*` flow in one direction. A module that needs something from a module it may not import uses a bridge instead.

## Direction

| Importer | May import | Must not import |
|---|---|---|
| `bifrost/`, `components/` | `bifrost/`, `components/` | any module |
| neutral modules (every module outside the engine, bpmn and dmn families: `solution-models`, `std`, `themes`, `git-cruiser`, `plugins`, `machine-sanctum`) | `bifrost/`, `components/`, any non-engine module | `engine-*` |
| bpmn modules (`bpmn-*`) | `bifrost/`, `components/`, neutral modules except `git-cruiser`, own family, **`dmn-core` only** from the dmn family | `engine-*`, `git-cruiser`, `dmn-*` other than `dmn-core` |
| dmn modules (`dmn-*`) | `bifrost/`, `components/`, neutral modules except `git-cruiser`, own family, **`bpmn-core` only** from the bpmn family | `engine-*`, `git-cruiser`, `bpmn-*` other than `bpmn-core` |
| engine modules (`engine-*`) | everything | — |

**Why the `-core` exception:** the Business Rule Task couples BPMN to DMN. Shared types and views that bridge the two families live in the family's `-core` module, so the other family may import them.

- `dmn-editor` may import `bpmn-core`, but not `bpmn-editor`, `bpmn-diff`, `bpmn-linter`, or `bpmn-token-simulator`.
- `bpmn-editor` may import `dmn-core`, but not `dmn-editor`, `dmn-diff`, or `dmn-decision-simulator`.

## Bridges

When the direction forbids an import, use one of:

- **Commands** — `bifrost.commands.executeCommand(...)`.
- **Mediator events** on shared mediators.
- **Contracts** in `bifrost/contracts/` — types, event names, IPC channel names, and registration interfaces (e.g. `PluginApiNamespace`, `MergeResolverHost`) that a module implements and the core consumes.

## Where generic code goes

| Kind | Location |
|---|---|
| Synchronous pure function | `bifrost/common/*Functions.ts` |
| React UI piece without module knowledge | `components/` |
| Async cross-module operation | a command in `std` |

**One-liner rule:** a one-line expression needed in several places is repeated, not extracted. Extract only when the logic is longer than one line or must stay identical.

## Enforcement

`studio/eslint.config.mjs` enforces the table with `no-restricted-imports` zones (`npm run lint:fix` fails on a violation). The dynamic `require` in `ModuleManager.ts` is not checked. Details: `docs/architecture/imports-and-modules.md` §Module Dependency Direction.
